00_pastry_shop:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  Program reads and prints a name that gets checked for lenght but is not printed as %s, so it can be used to read the stack and get the canary. 
  Then reads 256B into 64B buf. 

01_fortune_cookie:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  Program reads 256B into 64B buffer, then prints OK (can be used to brute force the canary, will print ok only if canary value was guessed right).

02_space_station:
  Canary enabled, PIE enabled, NX enabled.
  We can use the first input to print stack values and leak both the canary and a PIE address.
  Then we use the vmmap base address and the leaked PIE address to get the PIE offset.
  We use cyclic input to get canary offset and RIP offset and we start the exploit (ret address and win address will need the offet added to them)

03_secret_library:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  We can use the first input to leak the canary position and then the canary value.
  Then we start to exploit.

04_cafe_menu:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  We can skip the canary by overwriting the struct index in order to write into RIP and not into the table.
  We need to fill the table (48B padding), then write the RIP address into struct index (RIP address is 71, found by trying all numbers starting from 68).
  Then write the win function address.
  The program will write the win function address into the RIP address.

05_weather_station:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  Brute forced everything. Canary offset by sending a number of "a" until canary breaks.
  Canary value with lab code.
  RIP offset by sending a number of win function addresses until it works.
